---
import Simple from '../layouts/Simple.astro';
import { site, wi } from '../data/site.js';
const updated = '29 September 2026';
---
<Simple schema={{ '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'Terms', url: 'https://prewarmed.org/terms/' }}
  title="Terms — prewarmed.org"
  description="The terms that apply to using prewarmed.org and to orders placed through it, which are fulfilled by Warm Inboxes."
  eyebrow="Legal" h1="Terms">
  <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

  <p>{site.disclosure} Using this site means accepting what follows.</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>prewarmed.org publishes research, comparisons and calculators about cold email infrastructure, and it sells nothing directly. Every order link sends you to <a href={wi('/', { page: 'terms', placement: 'body' })} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Warm Inboxes</a>, where the purchase happens under that company's terms. If those terms and these ever disagree about an order, theirs govern the order.</p>

  <h2>What we say about prices and specifications</h2>
  <p>Prices shown here are published from a single data file and are kept in step with Warm Inboxes deliberately, but the price you pay is the one shown at checkout there. Specifications — aging and warming periods, mailbox counts, delivery times — describe what is normally supplied and are not a warranty for any individual order.</p>

  <h2>What we do not promise</h2>
  <p>Nobody can guarantee inbox placement, and we do not. Infrastructure decides whether your mail gets a fair hearing; your list, your copy and your sending behaviour decide the rest. Figures on this site — recommended volumes, aging periods, the arithmetic in the calculators — are guidance drawn from operating this infrastructure, not a prediction of your results.</p>
  <p>The free tools are provided as they are. Most of them run on warminboxes.com and are subject to that site's terms. Use their output as evidence, not as a verdict.</p>

  <h2>Using the site properly</h2>
  <p>You may read, quote and link to anything here. You may not scrape it wholesale, republish it as your own, or use it to build a competing directory. If you want to cite a figure, cite it and link back — that is encouraged.</p>
  <p>Infrastructure bought through the links here must be used lawfully. That means honouring unsubscribe requests, sending to data you have a lawful basis to contact, and complying with the rules that apply where you and your recipients are — CAN-SPAM, GDPR and PECR among them. Cold email is legal in most places when done properly. Doing it improperly is your liability, not ours.</p>

  <h2>Affiliate and commercial relationships</h2>
  <p>Some outbound links on this site are commercial, including every link to Warm Inboxes, which is operated by the same team. Where a link to a third party earns a commission, that is disclosed on the page it appears on. It never changes what we write about a product.</p>

  <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
  <p>We get things wrong sometimes. When a figure here is wrong, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a> and we will correct it and say what changed rather than editing quietly. The method behind the numbers is on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses arising from decisions you make based on this site — including lost revenue, lost data, or damage to a sending domain. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>These terms can change. The date at the top shows when they last did.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a>. Registered entity details are available on request to the same address.</p>
</Simple>
